        "comments": "The assembly rPodPit1.hap1.2 is based on 23x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Wellcome Sanger Institute Tree of Life Programme (https://www.sanger.ac.uk/programme/tree-of-life/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Sex chromosomes were assigned by synteny to Podarcis raffonei (GCA_027172205.1) and by PacBio reads coverage observed in the HiC map.\n\nStructural annotation is propagated from INSDC submissions or other annotation providers and processed to follow RefSeq standards. Functional annotation is provided by RefSeq, and is derived from model organism databases, orthologous species, curation, domain architecture analysis, and submitted information.",
